<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-J.Hardie year net profit soars.</title>
<headline>RTRS-J.Hardie year net profit soars.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>		  (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     70.0 vs 70.8</p>
<p>    Net profit			     83.0 vs 32.2</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		6.5 vs  6.5</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     13.0 vs 13.0</p>
<p>NOTE: James Hardie Industries Ltd is a building materials manufacturer and is about 28 percent owned by Australian Consolidated Investments Ltd, which in turn is controlled by Brierley Investments Ltd.  </p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			1.63 vs 1.75</p>
<p>    Other income			  497.3 vs 110.8</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    21.2 vs  8.3</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		   loss 0.4 vs loss 48.7</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date July 4</p>
<p>Reg date June 20</p>
<p>    Tax					13.1 vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Interest				 52.6 vs 68.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   86.6 vs 76.7</p>
</text>
